{"name":"Tardis","hex":"#105673","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tardis","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative form of TARDIS (time machine from the series Doctor Who which is larger on the inside than the outside)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something which resembles such a machine, either in that it travels through time or in that its interior is or appears to be larger (or more full of information or things) than its exterior suggested."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tardis"}],"entries":[{"title":"TARDIS","blocks":[{"text":"The TARDIS is a fictional hybrid of a time machine and spacecraft that has, since 1963, appeared in the British science fiction television series Doctor Who and its various spin-offs. While a TARDIS is capable of disguising itself, the exterior appearance of the Doctor's TARDIS typically mimics a police box, an obsolete type of telephone kiosk that was once commonly seen on streets in Britain in the 1940s and 50s. Its interior is shown as being much larger than its exterior, commonly described as being \"bigger on the inside\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Tardis_in_Snow.jpg/330px-Tardis_in_Snow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TARDIS","wikidata":"Q35684"},{"title":"TARDIS (software)","blocks":[{"text":"TARDIS, Temperature And Radiative Diffusion In Supernovae, is an open-source 1D Monte Carlo radiative-transfer spectral synthesis program used for numerical modelling and analysis of supernovae."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TARDIS_(software)","wikidata":"Q124372683"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Ilford_Manor_Road_geograph-3065865-by-Ben-Brooksbank.jpg/500px-Ilford_Manor_Road_geograph-3065865-by-Ben-Brooksbank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https: